# Elephant toothpaste: catalyst dose changes how fast the foam arrives
#
# Simulation activity. A real child-facing activity uses only household 3%
# hydrogen peroxide, adult supervision, fitted goggles and gloves. Potassium
# iodide demonstrations belong on a supervised school bench; stronger peroxide
# is virtual exploration here, not a home instruction.
register lv1

# A fair comparison: equal peroxide, soap, vessels and elapsed time. Only the
# potassium iodide dose changes. The catalyst is retained in both vessels.
add v1 Wasserstoffperoxid_3% 100mL
add v1 Spülmittel 10mL
add v1 KI 0.25g

new beaker
add v2 Wasserstoffperoxid_3% 100mL
add v2 Spülmittel 10mL
add v2 KI 1g

# One shared clock lets the first-order iodide dependence reach the visible
# gas/foam model without giving either vessel extra reaction time.
wait 10s
inspect v1
inspect v2

# Prediction: v2 should make more oxygen, build a taller foam column and spill
# farther in the same ten seconds. Neither vessel consumes its KI inventory.
